.TH BC250\-MON 1 "2026-09-07" "bc250-mon 0.1.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
bc250\-mon \- terminal sensor and hardware monitor for the AMD BC\-250
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bc250\-mon
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bc250\-mon
displays the hardware state of the AMD BC\-250 board (Cyan Skillfish APU,
gfx1013) in a terminal. It combines the layout familiar from
.BR btop (1)
\(em panels with bars and graphs \(em with a complete sensor table in the style
of HWiNFO, listing the current value of every channel alongside the minimum,
maximum and average observed since the program started.
.PP
The program uses only the Python standard library and
.B writes nothing:
it reads
.IR /sys ,
.I /proc
and
.IR /sys/class/hwmon .
It does not interfere with the GPU governor, CoolerControl, or the scripts that
unlock CPU cores and compute units.
.PP
On hardware other than a BC\-250 the program falls back to a generic mode: it
shows the sensors it actually finds and omits advice about hardware that is not
present.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fISEC\fR"
Refresh interval in seconds. Defaults to 1.0. In interactive mode it can be
changed with
.B +
and
.BR - .
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print a one\-shot text report and exit. The format is convenient for pasting
into bug reports.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a snapshot of the state as JSON and exit. Intended for scripts and for
logging over time.
.TP
.B \-\-lang " \fIpl\fR|\fIen\fR"
Interface language. Without this option the language comes from the
.B BC250_LANG
variable, and failing that from the system locale; anything unrecognised falls
back to English.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Run a simulated BC\-250 instead of reading hardware. Useful for previewing the
interface and for developing the program on a machine that is not a BC\-250.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-diagnostics
Start without the Diagnostics panel. The
.B d
key shows or hides it at any time.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short description of the options.
.SH VIEWS
.SS Dashboard
Panels for the GPU, CPU, motherboard and memory. Bars have one\-eighth\-character
resolution, history graphs are drawn with Braille characters, and colour follows
the temperature thresholds. Each panel shows several traces at once \(em for the
GPU that is temperature, power and clock \(em rather than one stretched graph.
On a tall window a condensed sensor table appears below the panels. At the
bottom a
.B Diagnostics
panel lists detected problems.
.PP
The CPU panel reports physical cores and threads as
.IR 8C/16T ,
which matters after a core unlock, when the number of logical CPUs alone is
misleading. If the thread list does not fit in the window, the program states
how many threads it omitted.
.SS Sensors
A table of every
.B hwmon
channel, grouped by chip, with the columns
.IR Now ,
.IR Min ,
.I Max
and
.IR Average .
The equivalent of the HWiNFO sensor window.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc
Quit.
.TP
.BR Tab ", " 1 ", " 2
Switch between the dashboard and the sensor table.
.TP
.BR \(ua " " \(da " " PgUp " " PgDn " " Home " " End
Scroll the sensor table.
.TP
.BR p ", " space
Pause refreshing.
.TP
.B r
Reset the collected minimums, maximums and averages.
.TP
.BR + ", " \-
Change the refresh interval by 0.25 s (range 0.25\(en10 s).
.TP
.BR h ", " ?
Help screen.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The program recognises known pitfalls of the BC\-250 board and, instead of
reporting misleading numbers, explains the cause:
.TP
.B GPU load unavailable
The amdgpu driver does not populate the activity field in
.IR gpu_metrics ;
bytes 0x1C\(en0x1D stay at 0xFFFF. This is the source of the well\-known
\(lq655%\(rq reading in MangoHud. The
.B cyan\-skillfish\-governor\-smu
service fixes it with its default
.I fix\-metrics
option.
.TP
.B GPU locked at 1500 MHz
The highest DPM level is 1500 MHz and no
.B cyan\-skillfish\-governor\-*
service is running. Without a governor the GPU will not scale above that
frequency.
.TP
.B pp_dpm_sclk reports nonsense
After unlocking eight CPU cores the kernel reports wrong clocks. When the whole
table is scaled down (for example
.I 15Mhz
instead of
.IR 1500Mhz )
the program multiplies it by 100 and flags the correction. When only the active
level is wrong (for example 98 MHz in a 1000\(en2000 MHz range) no factor fits,
so the GPU clock is taken from the averaged field of
.IR gpu_metrics ,
and with a governor configuration also estimated from vddgfx on the governor's
voltage curve. The GPU itself runs normally \(em this is a reporting bug, not a
performance one.
.TP
.B SuperIO module
Distinguishes
.B nct6683
(read\-only) from
.B nct6687
(read and write, including PWM) and reminds you which one fan control requires.
.TP
.B Temperature thresholds
GPU 85/90 \(deC, CPU 80/90 \(deC, NVMe 70/80 \(deC \(em warning and critical
values taken from the BC\-250 community documentation.
.TP
.B Fans at 0 RPM
With the SuperIO module loaded this usually means a fan connected outside the
monitored J1 and J4003 headers, or a fan mode set in the BIOS.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/class/drm/card*/device/
amdgpu card data: PCI identifier,
.IR pp_dpm_sclk ,
.IR pp_dpm_mclk ,
.IR gpu_metrics ,
.IR gpu_busy_percent ,
.IR mem_info_vram_* ,
.IR power_dpm_force_performance_level .
.TP
.I /sys/class/hwmon/hwmon*/
Temperatures, voltages, fan speeds, PWM and power draw from the amdgpu,
k10temp, nct6686 and nvme chips.
.TP
.I /proc/stat ", " /proc/meminfo ", " /proc/loadavg ", " /proc/modules
Per\-core load, memory, system load average, loaded modules.
.TP
.I /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/
Current CPU clocks, governor and driver names, and the topology used to count
physical cores.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BC250_LANG
Interface language
.RI ( pl
or
.IR en )
when
.B \-\-lang
is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
An interactive monitor refreshed twice a second:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-mon \-i 0.5
.EE
.RE
.PP
A report for a bug report:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-mon \-\-once > bc250\-state.txt
.EE
.RE
.PP
Logging GPU temperature every five seconds:
.PP
.RS
.EX
while sleep 5; do bc250\-mon \-\-json | jq \-r '[now, .gpu.temp_c, .gpu.power_w] | @csv'; done
.EE
.RE
.PP
Previewing the interface without a BC\-250 board:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-mon \-\-demo
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Finished normally.
.TP
.B 2
No interactive terminal when started without
.B \-\-once
or
.BR \-\-json .
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.9 or newer. Board sensors require a loaded SuperIO module:
.B modprobe nct6687 force=true
(full access including PWM) or
.B modprobe nct6683 force=true
(read\-only).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sensors (1),
.BR btop (1),
.BR nvtop (1),
.BR radeontop (1),
.BR bc250-nosuspend (1)
.PP
